    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has length $\\frac{5x}{4}$ m and width $\\frac{3x}{4}$ m. What is the area of the rectangle? Find the area if $x=12$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{15x^2}{16}\\text{ m}^2$; when $x=12$, $135\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "worked": "Using $A=lw$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{5x}{4}\\times\\frac{3x}{4}\\\\A&=\\frac{15x^2}{16}\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=12$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{15\\times12^2}{16}\\\\A&=\\frac{2160}{16}\\\\A&=135\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
